Use the native CONFIG_SITE ABI flags for Autoconf dependencies.

libzvbi configure fails with an empty include filename when shell-quoted
CMake flags reach Clang literally. Nettle and GnuTLS use the same flag
construction. The native CONFIG_SITE compiler commands already provide the
launcher, forced ABI header and stdio overlay; keep the platform defines
without duplicating those options in Autoconf flag strings.

Upstream: PS5-only; requires the native catalogue's shared CONFIG_SITE.

--- a/depends/common/libzvbi/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/depends/common/libzvbi/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -4,8 +4,8 @@
 # Keep the target architecture, SDK and deployment flags supplied by Kodi.
 list(APPEND zvbi_conf "CC=${CMAKE_C_COMPILER}"
                       "CXX=${CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER}"
-                      "CFLAGS=${CMAKE_C_FLAGS}"
-                      "CXXFLAGS=${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS}"
+                      "CFLAGS=-DTARGET_POSIX -DTARGET_FREEBSD"
+                      "CXXFLAGS=-DTARGET_POSIX -DTARGET_FREEBSD"
                       "CPPFLAGS=-I${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/include $ENV{CPPFLAGS}"
                       "LDFLAGS=-L${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/lib ${CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS} $ENV{LDFLAGS}")
 if(HOST)
